<p class="max-w-xl mt-4">
  The "Polimoney" project was launched to solve problems around politics and money from the bottom up, modeled on the highly transparent system for running politics used in Sweden.
</p>
<section>
  <h3 class="text-2xl mt-10">The Swedish example</h3>
  <p class="mt-4">
    In Sweden, politicians and public officials are issued official credit cards and are required to use them for public spending. The system is designed for transparency: every expense is recorded and can be accessed by the public and the media.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4">
    By bringing a similar system to Japan, we aim to reduce the administrative cost of handling political funds and to make transparent, trustworthy politics happen from the bottom up.
  </p>
</section>
<section>
  <h3 class="text-2xl mt-10">How to adopt it</h3>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Please contact us via the <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScytDD9cdYwcl_Gsr0qal-Op7mpXaQzK3KGTk_FsahY5FkU9w/viewform" hreflang="ja">Google Form (Japanese)</a>.
  </p>
</section>
<section>
  <h3 class="text-2xl mt-10">Next steps</h3>
  <p class="mt-4">
    We are also developing "Polimoney Ledger", accounting software for political and election campaign funds that can output income and expenditure reports (or supporting CSV files for making them) and files compatible with Polimoney.
  </p>
</section>
